  "body": "⭕ After you discover 1 or more clues from a non-basic investigate action: Look at the top 2 cards of the encounter deck. You may choose 1 to place on the bottom of the encounter deck. Return the rest to the top of the encounter deck in any order. (Limit once per round.)\n⭐ effect: +0. Choose and discard a non-weakness treachery card in the threat area of an investigator at your location.",
  "flavor": "",
  "illustrator": "Aleksander Karcz",
  "card_number": "4",
  "encounter_group_number": "",
  "picture_base64": "data:image/jpeg;base64,",
  "image_mode": 1,
  "back": {
    "name": "🏅Daisy Walker",
    "subtitle": "The Librarian",
    "class": "探求者",
    "card_back": {
      "other": "【Deckbuilding Options】: Seeker cards (🔍) level 0-5, up to five Mystic (🧘) cards level 0-1, up to five Survivor (🏕️) cards level 0-1, Neutral cards level 0-5.\n【Deckbuilding Requirements】 (do not count toward deck size): Daisy’s Tote Bag, The Necronomicon (John Dee Translation), 1 random basic weakness.",
      "story": "As a respected librarian at Miskatonic University, Daisy had always felt that books were the most important thing in her life. She explored in fiction what she abhorred in life: horror, violence, fear. Then, she stumbled across the John Dee translation of the Necronomicon. It was blasphemous, unholy, and too awful to be read. But given her studies in obscure and occult subjects, Daisy knew there was more truth than fiction within the book's pages. She began to wonder what other secrets the restricted collection of the Orne Library held...",
      "size": 30
    },
